  "rationale": "Blocking iotDevice:exploitPublicApp removes memoryDump and everything that depends on it: printServer, rdpLogin, monitoringHost, vpnSession, serviceAccount and secretsManager. That cuts off mailArchive, dbReplica and shareMount. vaultRead stays reachable only through appServer:lateralMovement, which is fed by configSecret (from containerHost) and by dbLogin. Blocking appServer:lateralMovement closes that last route. One block is not enough: the appServer path through configSecret and the printServer path through iotDevice share no common step, so no single block cuts both. The minimum is 2."
 },
